From c0097d3ede7d4090c53ac0d7464496c2473ebe48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:39:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xad: interpret LhA protection extensions by their type

LhAParseExt stores extensions 0x40 (MS-DOS attributes) and 0x50 (UNIX
mode) in prot, but normally interprets that value using the archive's
OS identifier. An Amiga archive carrying a UNIX mode is therefore
converted as Amiga protection bits.

Set the conversion discriminator with each explicit extension: MS-DOS
for 0x40, UNIX for 0x50. If both occur, the last recognized extension
still wins, but its value and type stay together. The base-header path
is unchanged when neither extension is present.

Tested on mainline ABIv1 x86_64 under QEMU with GCC 10.5.0.
Compared this isolated change and the unmodified parser over 18 generated
level 1/2 archives; all probe exit codes were 0. Target metadata is
correct and unrelated fixture output is unchanged.
Repository: contrib (https://github.com/aros-development-team/contrib.git)
Base: 6bbefa406c281909294c4c4e8743f7f892caa1cf
Requires: none
Scope: XAD LhA level 1 and 2 metadata decoding
Upstream-Status: submitted (https://github.com/aros-development-team/contrib/pull/81)
Verification: mainline ABIv1 x86_64, GCC 10.5.0, QEMU; 18 metadata fixtures and unchanged controls. See docs/upstream-xad-lha.md.
Removal: retire after the application pin includes the accepted upstream change

---
 workbench/libs/xad/portable/clients/LhA.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/workbench/libs/xad/portable/clients/LhA.c b/workbench/libs/xad/portable/clients/LhA.c
index e99b94de..8b89daa3 100644
--- a/workbench/libs/xad/portable/clients/LhA.c
+++ b/workbench/libs/xad/portable/clients/LhA.c
@@ -172,9 +172,12 @@ struct xadMasterBase *xadMasterBase)
             err = XADERR_NOMEMORY;
         }
         break;
-      case 0x40:
-        if (os == 0) os = 'M'; // force OS ID for MS-DOS protection bits
-      case 0x50: /* File permission */
+      case 0x40: /* MS-DOS attributes override the base-header attributes */
+        os = 'M';
+        prot = EndGetI16(&bufptr[1]);
+        break;
+      case 0x50: /* UNIX mode, independent of the archive's OS identifier */
+        os = 'U';
         prot = EndGetI16(&bufptr[1]);
         break;
       case 0x51: /* ID's */
